 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met. Two settings on two different scenes were confirmed as challenging, and only one of them is a clear policy failure. On 096988dd, the car 1 s early at 2x speed with the ego at 1.2x (S5) failed every run: the policy drifted left out of its lane into car 41 alongside it. On 1c45ce3a, the car 2 s late at 2x speed with the ego at 0.8x (S34) also failed every run, but triage blames a replayed car (24) cutting into the slowed ego, so that failure comes from replay rather than from a clear policy mistake. The strongest third candidate is 187e6244 with the lead car 1.5 s late at 0.75x and the ego at 0.8x (S31). The policy drove into the lead car there, but the range still straddles 0.5, so it is not confirmed. The other six scenes never failed, though most of their settings got only one run, which is a hint and not a rate.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "The 096988dd case is confirmed and the policy is at fault. At 1 s early, 2x car speed and 1.2x ego speed, every run failed the same way: under a STRAIGHT or RIGHT command the planned path bent left and the ego's front corner hit car 41 passing in the left lane.",
